in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @nl
in @time

# @time/format — the projection-to-string species of @time.
#
# Species under @time at the projection-to-string altitude. Landed
# 2026-07-23 by Reed per Seam Phase D 6876699 Mint B forward-promise
# discharge + Taut `173a1204` §5 vocabulary gap remediation (main.rs
# `current_utc_timestamp` + `format_utc_iso8601` + `is_leap` ~55 LOC
# E-bucket lift target blocked on @time/format species).
#
# Format IS the projection of a @time value → string representation
# for @io emission (log lines, observation crystals, cli output). Not
# a new mechanism; a substrate-decl'd carrier for the projection-shape.
#
# === Substrate authority ===
#
# - **Family-root**: `shards/time.mirror` (Mara Round 2, 2026-07-20)
# - **Sibling species** (landed same tick as family-root):
#     @time/past    — the past-light-cone temporal region
#     @time/now     — the observer's current spacetime event
#     @time/future  — the future-light-cone temporal region
# - **This species (@time/format)** is the FOURTH sibling under @time,
#   distinct from the three light-cone regions in that it names the
#   projection-operator, not a temporal region.
# - **Composes over**: @time carrier (input) + string carrier (output);
#   @nl for literal-string help/documentation
# - **Consumer** (post-mint): `rust/src/main.rs` helpers currently
#   embedded in Bucket E scaffolding — the lift retires ~55 LOC of
#   time-formatting utilities into shard-body composition via
#   apply_h::act arms dispatching to this species' actions.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit (clean) ===
#
# The word `format` audit:
#
# - No prior `format.mirror` shard exists at any altitude across
#   shards/ (grep clean 2026-07-23)
# - No format collision at @time altitude (past/now/future are
#   temporal-region species; format is a projection-operator species)
# - `format` word used generically in `shards/nl.mirror` for
#   @nl.compose variants; different altitude, different domain (nl-
#   string composition vs time-value projection)
#
# Grep verdict CLEAN for this species altitude.
#
# === The format shapes ===
#
# ISO-8601 is the canonical wire format at cli + log + observation-
# crystal altitude per @spectral/signature + @uuid/spectral/time
# precedents. Other formats declared at species altitude for
# projection flexibility; Rust runtime realization dispatches through
# `apply_h::act` arms per bilateral discharge.
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/time/format.mirror`
# declares `@time/format` and only that.

prism @time/format {
  focus  format
  project format
  split  format
  shift  format
  settle format
}

# === iso8601 — the canonical wire format ===
#
# iso8601(t: time) -> str
#
# Project a @time value to ISO-8601 string representation
# (YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.mmmmmmZ). Substrate-decl'd carrier; runtime
# realization via std::time / chrono formatting at the phone.rs
# boundary.
#
# Body `\`-obligation-blocked per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]];
# consumers pull realization via `apply_h::act` bilateral resolver-
# arm dispatch (task #140 landing).
iso8601(t: ref) -> ref { \ }

# === unix — numerical timestamp ===
#
# unix(t: time) -> int
#
# Project a @time value to Unix timestamp (seconds since
# 1970-01-01T00:00Z). For numerical comparison + hashing contexts.
unix(t: ref) -> ref { \ }

# === rfc3339 — JSON-adjacent wire format ===
#
# rfc3339(t: time) -> str
#
# Project a @time value to RFC 3339 string representation (subset of
# ISO-8601; widely used in JSON APIs and structured-log formats).
rfc3339(t: ref) -> ref { \ }

# === Bilateral predicates ===

# format_is_roundtrippable(t: time, s: str) -> verdict
#
# Discharges Pass iff formatting t to s via iso8601/rfc3339, then
# parsing s back, produces a @time value byte-equal to t. Substrate-
# honest sanity check for the projection at the lossless-format
# altitude.
bilateral format_is_roundtrippable {
  sentinel "time-format=roundtrippable=parse-of-format-yields-input"
  arity 2
}
format_is_roundtrippable(t: ref, s: ref) -> verdict { \ }

out @time/format
out iso8601
out unix
out rfc3339
out format_is_roundtrippable
